Community reserve fund dividend launched, 43% token pool benefits ecological participants

@WalrusProtocol  officially activates the 2026 community reserve fund dividend plan, derived from the 43% total supply community reserve pool that will distribute profits quarterly. This dividend covers three groups: staked users, governance participants, and ecological developers, where staked users account for 60% of the dividend, governance voting users account for 25%, and developers' contributions account for 15%. As of January, the first quarter dividend pool has gathered protocol fees and storage service fees exceeding 21 million WAL. At the current exchange rate of 1 WAL = 0.13 USD, the dividend pool is valued at over 2.73 million USD. Dividends do not require manual claims and will be automatically distributed to eligible accounts.
